{"seq":34,"data":{"type":"RUN_FINISHED","threadId":"c3a0d747-3b27-41a6-80e6-f2dcac2353eb","runId":"run_1_1788506492768","result":"Perfect! I've created the regex pattern and saved it to `/app/regex.txt`. \n\nThe regex works as follows:\n\n1. **Line start with IPv4 check**: `^(?=.*\\b...\\b)` - Ensures the line contains a valid IPv4 address using lookahead\n2. **IPv4 pattern**: Matches each octet as 0-255 without leading zeros (e.g., `192` matches, but `01` or `001` don't)\n3. **Date capture with proper ranges**:\n   - Months 01,03,05,07,08,10,12: days 01-31\n   - Months 04,06,09,11: days 01-30  \n   - February: days 01-29\n4. **Last date matching**: The negative lookahead `(?![^\\n]*\\bDATE\\b)` ensures no other date follows on the same line\n5. **Word boundaries**: `\\b` around dates and IPv4 prevent partial matches and false positives like \"user1134-12-1234\"\n\nWhen used with `re.findall(pattern, log_text, re.MULTILINE)`, it will return only the captured date strings from lines containing IPv4 addresses.","rawEvent":{"duration_api_ms":119778,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"c3a0d747-3b27-41a6-80e6-f2dcac2353eb","total_cost_usd":0.12042710000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":17,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19008,"cache_read_input_tokens":26321,"output_tokens":18555,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":17445},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":19008},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":8,"output_tokens":564,"cache_read_input_tokens":13632,"cache_creation_input_tokens":18065,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":18065,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":1158,"outputTokens":17,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.001243,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutpu